// What `us` does not know about a sole proprietor: the business's profit,
// self-employment tax, the qualified business income deduction, and the check on
// the 1040-ES installments. Each one counts into a line `us` reads (total-income,
// adjustments, deductions, other-taxes), so `us` needs no copy and no file name
// matters: a law that reads a tally runs after every law that counts into it.
//
// Simplified: no QBI wage or property limits (income is far below the
// threshold), no state tax, no underpayment penalty.

// ─── The return ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Schedule C: net profit is receipts less business expenses, and it is income
/// (IRC §61(a)(2)). Receipts count when the money arrives, expenses when they
/// are recognized.
///
/// To fix: `axiom why net-profit` lists the receipts and the expenses behind it.
law business-profit
  each year closing 04-15
  let net = value(tally(gross-receipts), USD) - value(tally(business-expenses), USD)
  count net as net-profit
  count net as total-income

/// Schedule SE: 12.4% Social Security up to the wage base and 2.9% Medicare, on
/// 92.35% of net earnings (IRC §1401). It is a tax on top of income tax, so it
/// counts into `other-taxes`, and half of it comes off income (IRC §164(f)).
///
/// To fix: the base is net profit; a loss owes nothing.
law self-employment-tax
  each year closing 04-15
  let earnings = max(value(tally(net-profit), USD), empty) * 92.35%
  let tax = min(earnings, ss-wage-base[year]) * 12.4% + earnings * 2.9%
  count tax as se-tax
  count tax as other-taxes
  count tax * 50% as se-deduction
  count tax * 50% as adjustments

/// The qualified business income deduction is 20% of the business's income after
/// what is attributable to it (half of self-employment tax, health premiums, the
/// SEP-IRA), limited to 20% of taxable income before it (IRC §199A). It is added
/// to the deduction `us` took.
///
/// To fix: the deduction cannot exceed a fifth of taxable income; a lower
/// deduction means less income before it.
law qbi-deduction
  each year closing 04-15
  let attributable = value(tally(net-profit), USD) - value(tally(se-deduction), USD) - value(tally(health-premiums), USD) - value(tally(sep-contributions), USD)
  let before = max(value(tally(agi), USD) - value(tally(deductions), USD), empty)
  count min(max(attributable, empty), before) * 20% as deductions


// ─── Estimated payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Form 1040-ES: four installments, each due on a fixed day. Paying 100% of last
// year's tax in four equal parts is the safe harbor from the underpayment
// penalty (IRC §6654(d)). A `by` law fires when the journal reaches its date and
// reads what has been paid for that year so far. Each names one day, so 2025's
// first three installments are three laws; the fourth falls in the next
// January, for the year that ended, which one law covers for every year: it
// closes on January 15 and reads the year it closes.

/// First installment, due April 15 2025.
///
/// To fix: pay the installment `for` the year to a place of kind `federal-tax`.
law estimate-1-2025
  by 2025-04-15
  warn value(tally(payments), USD) >= prior-year-tax[2025] * 25% "estimated tax: first installment short"

/// Second installment. June 15 2025 fell on a Sunday, so it was due Monday the 16th.
///
/// To fix: pay the installment `for` the year to a place of kind `federal-tax`.
law estimate-2-2025
  by 2025-06-16
  warn value(tally(payments), USD) >= prior-year-tax[2025] * 50% "estimated tax: second installment short"

/// Third installment, due September 15 2025.
///
/// To fix: pay the installment `for` the year to a place of kind `federal-tax`.
law estimate-3-2025
  by 2025-09-15
  warn value(tally(payments), USD) >= prior-year-tax[2025] * 75% "estimated tax: third installment short"

/// The fourth installment of any year is due on January 15 of the next, and pays
/// what is still short of the safe harbor. It is `for` the year that ended, so
/// this law reads that year's payments on the day it closes.
///
/// To fix: pay the installment `for` the year to a place of kind `federal-tax`.
law estimate-4
  each year closing 01-15
  warn value(tally(payments), USD) >= prior-year-tax[year] * 100% "estimated tax: fourth installment short"


// ─── Figures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The Social Security wage base (SSA, October 2024 and October 2025 releases).
param ss-wage-base
  2025 176_100 USD
  2026 184_500 USD

// The SEP-IRA dollar cap (IRC §415(c)).
param sep-limit
  2025 70_000 USD
  2026 72_000 USD

// The share of the home used for work.
param office-share
  2025 15%

// Last year's total tax, from that year's return: the safe-harbor amount.
param prior-year-tax
  2025 9_200 USD
  2026 11_301.28 USD
